{
  "_comment": "Producer-minted policy.resolve contract vectors. Each vector's request is executed against the live dispatch in policy_ops tests and the reply/error asserted byte-equal, so these bytes ARE the wire contract. Consumers (subc-client-rs policy_cache) vendor this file under the digest-pin discipline. Subject placeholders: {AGENT_ID} is substituted with the seeded agent's id at test time; every other byte is literal. Reply revision is the CURRENT global policy generation at resolve time (the cache watermark), never the matched rule's write-time stamp - all vectors resolve against a store whose generation is 3. Complete verdict vocabulary: rules carry allow | deny | ask (closed at authoring per domain); replies additionally serve deny (policy-less approval default) and deny_unknown_domain (undeclared domain marker). ask is the attended-parking verdict: consumers park attended callers and treat unattended refusal-to-proceed as transient-fault per the cascade spec.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "agent_subject_allow",
      "request": {
        "domain": "approval",
        "gate_id": "plexus.github_write",
        "subject": {
          "agent_id": "{AGENT_ID}"
        },
        "project_root": "/repo"
      },
      "reply": {
        "verdict": "allow",
        "revision": 3,
        "ttl_ms": 30000
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "session_subject_allow",
      "request": {
        "domain": "approval",
        "gate_id": "plexus.github_write",
        "subject": {
          "session_id": "ses_vectors"
        },
        "project_root": "/repo"
      },
      "reply": {
        "verdict": "allow",
        "revision": 3,
        "ttl_ms": 30000
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "deny_rule",
      "request": {
        "domain": "approval",
        "gate_id": "plexus.reactions",
        "subject": {
          "session_id": "ses_vectors"
        },
        "project_root": "/repo"
      },
      "reply": {
        "verdict": "deny",
        "revision": 3,
        "ttl_ms": 30000
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ask_rule_attended_parking_verdict",
      "request": {
        "domain": "approval",
        "gate_id": "plexus.issue_comment",
        "subject": {
          "session_id": "ses_vectors"
        },
        "project_root": "/repo"
      },
      "reply": {
        "verdict": "ask",
        "revision": 3,
        "ttl_ms": 30000
      }
    },
